{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city","id":1543375,"title":"How many Cursed in a city?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-08T17:53:19-07:00","id":1543375,"title":"How many Cursed in a city?","content":"When the game talks about family hierarchy, and family heads, is it talking globally, or per city? If each family has enough member in a city to form a hierarchy with it's own leaders, that must mean there are hundreds of Cursed in every city. Or will a city only have one or two of each family? Do members of different families group together to form organizations, like the Covenants/Packs/Freeholds/etc? Or does each family pretty much keep to itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T19:25:09-07:00","id":1543378,"title":"","content":"As always, the general rule is &quot;However much is needed to make the game work.&quot; If Curseborne has learned any lessons from it's predeccesors, we're never going to get an exact answer for how many Accursed is in any given setting asides from the absolute most broadest generalizations<br /> <br /> Going into more specific idea, So far Chapter 1 and the Lineages have been a little vague about how they interact with increasing spatial scope-games are set for an idea of being local in the corebook, and that most of your shit is the result of dealing with the local iterations of Families and other Organizations, but Families like The Wardens, House Bathory, and Z.E.D &amp; Colleagues are described as being not only large enough but centralized enough that it assumes a global setup, of which local versions are explicitly branches of the larger Family.<br /> <br /> I imagine future sourcebooks, including the undoubted ones focusing specifically on the Lineages, and I imagine we'll get touches on explanation in the Storytelling chapter.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, the general vibe I would say I've taken is that Families describe the most global, top-down view on them but that most Families that don't particularly mention hierarchy or centrality are mostly defined by their local branch rather than being solely driven by that view, whereas those that do mention hierarchy/centrality are much more uniform across various settings. And as taht relates to populations.<br /> <br /> Well, back to the &quot;How many do you need?&quot; answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T06:25:37-07:00","id":1543418,"title":"","content":"To borrow from the manuscript, how many raccoons are in your city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T08:25:44-07:00","id":1543427,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, it's &quot;how many do you need?&quot; The number of times the Vampire sidebar that referenced the 1:100,000 Kindred/human ratio caused interminable debates has convinced me to never state an average for Curseborne or any other game I work on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T11:11:04-07:00","id":1543432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543418#post1543418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To borrow from the manuscript, how many raccoons are in your city?</div> </div> </div> </div>As this fandom grows, we need to make sure cultivating &quot;how many racoons are in your city?&quot; as an answer to this question is done, excellent quotation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-09-2024, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:18:30-07:00","id":1543634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city#post1543375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the game talks about family hierarchy, and family heads, is it talking globally, or per city? If each family has enough member in a city to form a hierarchy with it's own leaders, that must mean there are hundreds of Cursed in every city. Or will a city only have one or two of each family? Do members of different families group together to form organizations, like the Covenants/Packs/Freeholds/etc? Or does each family pretty much keep to itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Raccoons aside I think there's a couple of legacy assumptions baked into this, one of which CB explicitly rejects and one of which I'm hoping it will reject. <br /> <br /> Assumption 1 is that there's any kind of *problem* with there bring hundreds of Accursed around in any given city. VtM was predicated on the Masquerade, he idea that nobody could ever find out that supernaturals are real or Bad Things Will Happen.<br /> <br /> CofD and Curseborne assume a much higher level of background weirdness. If Curseborne in particular the assumption seems to be that most people have actually encountered the supernatural at some point, even if just in the form of a Liminal Space or, well, a Curse.<br /> <br /> Assumption 2 (and this is the one I *hope* they hard break from) is that the City is the base unit of the setting. It only really made sense for VtM and got stranger and stranger the more dimension hopping the games started to involve.<br /> <br /> By default, the game is set in the modern world. People can travel, use phones, send emails. Cities don't need to be these isolated fiefdoms. Even if there's only one Zed locally, for example, they can still get backup from the branch office two towns over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:48:15-07:00","id":1543660,"title":"","content":"As old <b>CoD</b> ST, when creating game, I just write the number of supernatural beings I need for stories and political reasons in area. ( At minimum it's like 20 NPCs, to cover at least one monster main types.) <b>VtM</b> numbers maybe good for more USA eyeballing, or first look, but in Europe it simply not work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I live in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lublin\" target=\"_blank\">City of <b>Lublin</b></a>, that is rather 9th largest city in Poland. ( We are capitol of <i>Wojew\u00f3dztwo</i>, sorta like USA State area. ) Lublin has circa 340 000 citizens - it would mean we would have <i><b>3.4 of monsters</b></i> by <b>VtM</b> rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 4 if we round up numbers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sorry, on 4 NPCs, even with 3-5 PCs I cannot make even smallest vampire domain or mages consillium. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If I remember my notes for game I prepared but not run - it was something like that:<ul><li>7 vampires</li> <li>Circa 30 mages ( Lublin is Collages city )</li> <li>Circa 20 changelings ( we have weird paganism and folklore rules, but also some people missing in area )</li> </ul>Not counting werewolves, as I was not sure if wanted to use them in story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And how will it all work in Lublin? Simply, <b>CoD</b> setting has many 'people are forgetting' mechanics for monsters - Masquerade enforcement for vamps, Delirium for wolves, Sleeping Curse for mages, etc. ALSO <u><b>CoD </b>directly assume EVERYONE had at least once in their life encounter with supernatural - only they repressed their memories.</u> ( See <b>CoD</b> 2E corebook. question <i>'What you forgotten?'</i> for new characters. )<br /> <br /> I assume <b>Curseborne</b> has similar assumptions even if we do not see it yet in the text. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Especially with much higher empathises on crossovers than <b>CoD.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2024, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T03:10:30-07:00","id":1543672,"title":"","content":"I lately watched <b>The Order</b> (2019) TV series - one of official Inspirational TV Media from <b>Curseborne</b> core. It's a story about mages titular Order ( Family in CB ) and werewolves pack on american collage campus. I suspect that even biggest collage campus do not have more than 100 000 citizens, 200 000 tops.<br /> <br /> In the <b>The Order</b> TV series we have this number of characters by supernatural subtypes on campus:<ul><li>3-5 werewolves ( it's fluctuating in story )</li> <li>Circa 30 mages ( in titular Order ) - at least 10 are first and second level story characters regular on screen</li> </ul>So the <b>VtM</b> numbers are simply bogus to use, when doing chronicle like 'tv series' in the end. \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f<br /> <br /> More appropriate would be like<b> 1</b><b>Curseborne per 20 000 mortals</b> - and those are only very rough and rounded down estimates. \ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-13-2024, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T16:36:53-07:00","id":1543714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543634#post1543634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raccoons aside I think there's a couple of legacy assumptions baked into this</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another problem (in the math sense) that was actually relevant in previous games, and I wish CB does it differently (idk, didn't read anything yet):<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators under pressure.<br /> <br /> However you frame them, both VtM and VtR vampires have a very important assumption about them: they need 1 unit of blood per night, every night. That, more even than any extra feeding to power their things, makes for an ecological pressure that\u2019s hard to ignore, especially when you know how much this harms humans.<br /> <br /> All the calculations about how many critters live in an area started from this single problem. You can (and arguably should) ignore it, but you will have it cross your mind at some point, and will have people asking questions with this in mind. How many vamps before the city crumbles under pure ecological pressure?<br /> <br /> If the Hunger need to eat a minimum amount of blood every day, then the problem will stay. You can expect this question to pop out time and again and realism will linger on it. But if they don\u2019t, and I think this works fine, then the whole debacle becomes irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T18:04:44-07:00","id":1543718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543634#post1543634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assumption 2 (and this is the one I *hope* they hard break from) is that the City is the base unit of the setting. It only really made sense for VtM and got stranger and stranger the more dimension hopping the games started to involve.<br /> <br /> By default, the game is set in the modern world. People can travel, use phones, send emails. Cities don't need to be these isolated fiefdoms. Even if there's only one Zed locally, for example, they can still get backup from the branch office two towns over.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's...the exact opposite of how it worked? World of Darkness was a lot more globally oriented on the whole, and if you could get over the individual limitations of travels that normally afflict lower powered characters (assuming such were in place, like with Masqeurade), the mechanics and politics of the setting quickly reveal themselves to cover whole swathes of continents that you could try and work with, at risk of getting jammed in and chewed up by them. There's a reason why if you were a unaffiliated Lasombra in a Camarilla region, you'd basically got set to get fucked.<br /> <br /> Chronicles, by contrast, was the really city-oriented style of play, where in even characters that had mass-distance travel more readily baked into their character designs weren't personally invested in doing so-changelings from Lost could theoretically wrestle the Hedge into letting them traverse the world on a low budget and low time-sink, but most changelings want to get home, and even those less picky about their old homes don't want to have to handle the Hedge all that long, and there's more benefit in picking a corner of reality and holing up there. Vampires in Requiem look at the globalization that was starting to happen with the Roman Empire tend to take the Fall of Rome as they experieneced as a warning sign against the practice of being more globally centralized and organized, or the disagreements about what they would have to accomodate for in trying it again becomes the backbone for why they more or less stay fractured (also nevermind how the difference between Generation and Blood Potency relates to why you could have a global conspiracy of vampires in the one game and could expect such to always fall apart in the other). The most powerful splats of Chronicles were the ones more marked by being World-like in terms of global scales for casual participants, but even then the Awakened, the Arisen, and the Unchained still had more reasons to work on the city level than the global level in opposition to World.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, Curseborne's main mention of scope being <i>personal</i>, as mentioned in another thread, seems like a answer toward's the either/or approach depicted by the former two, because while that readily translates to a local frame, <i>personal</i> is flexible to the character. If you've got a world-trotting character, then so long as that attempt at world-trotting isn't an attempt to escape the personal scope, then Curseborne is happy work with you. It helps that the Families both seem to be structural enough that connections are easy to come up with without being so omnipresent that their presence or absence sets hard boundaries for anything else-you can design a local area however you want without feeling like it's divorced from the rest of the setting or needing to answer why there *isn't* a unified collective on the global scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-13-2024, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T19:04:00-07:00","id":1543723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543714#post1543714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's another problem (in the math sense) that was actually relevant in previous games, and I wish CB does it differently (idk, didn't read anything yet):<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators under pressure.<br /> <br /> However you frame them, both VtM and VtR vampires have a very important assumption about them: they need 1 unit of blood per night, every night. That, more even than any extra feeding to power their things, makes for an ecological pressure that\u2019s hard to ignore, especially when you know how much this harms humans.<br /> <br /> All the calculations about how many critters live in an area started from this single problem. You can (and arguably should) ignore it, but you will have it cross your mind at some point, and will have people asking questions with this in mind. How many vamps before the city crumbles under pure ecological pressure?<br /> <br /> If the Hunger need to eat a minimum amount of blood every day, then the problem will stay. You can expect this question to pop out time and again and realism will linger on it. But if they don\u2019t, and I think this works fine, then the whole debacle becomes irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this opens a bit of a can of worms.<br /> <br /> By current manuscript rules, Hungry need to feed once per game session. If each session covers an hour of game time, they need to feed once an hour, they cover weeks, they need to feed once every few weeks. <br /> <br /> And different Hungry have different Hungers. All *can* drink blood but some eat flesh, some eat hearts, some drain memories and some devour souls. <br /> <br /> The intentional game design is that how this all works is up to the players. There has been a fair bit of pushback against quite how vague it is. I'm personally in the camp that is fine with things being up to the players as long as its explicitly stated as a rule rather than being something you have to infer from flavour text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T19:22:40-07:00","id":1543724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543714#post1543714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's another problem (in the math sense) that was actually relevant in previous games, and I wish CB does it differently (idk, didn't read anything yet):<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators under pressure.<br /> <br /> However you frame them, both VtM and VtR vampires have a very important assumption about them: they need 1 unit of blood per night, every night. That, more even than any extra feeding to power their things, makes for an ecological pressure that\u2019s hard to ignore, especially when you know how much this harms humans.<br /> <br /> All the calculations about how many critters live in an area started from this single problem. You can (and arguably should) ignore it, but you will have it cross your mind at some point, and will have people asking questions with this in mind. How many vamps before the city crumbles under pure ecological pressure?<br /> <br /> If the Hunger need to eat a minimum amount of blood every day, then the problem will stay. You can expect this question to pop out time and again and realism will linger on it. But if they don\u2019t, and I think this works fine, then the whole debacle becomes irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The write-ups we have so far make no stipulation of about required &quot;top-offs&quot; to keep from Damnation, so it's not like vampires in the previous gamelines.<br /> <br /> But honestly, the answer remains &quot;how much versimilitude is enough for your play group?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T19:23:53-07:00","id":1543725,"title":"","content":"<br /> The game\u2019s family hierarchy can operate both globally and locally. Some cities might only have a few members of each family, while others could have enough to establish full hierarchies. Families may either keep to themselves or collaborate with others, forming larger organizations like Covenants or Packs. Whether they work together or stay isolated depends on the families' traditions and goals. <div align=\"right\"><a href=\"https://retrobowlgame.io\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">retro bowl</span></a></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28615-anthonyhood","name":"anthonyhood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T21:56:49-07:00","id":1543730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543723#post1543723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By current manuscript rules, Hungry need to feed once per game session. If each session covers an hour of game time, they need to feed once an hour, they cover weeks, they need to feed once every few weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhere in <b>CoD</b> 2E or <b>Scions</b> 2E books it was established that '<b>1 game session = 1 day of game time</b>', more or less.<br /> <br /> You can very taxing game sessions - like yesterday I run intense fights in <b>Trinity</b> - but even those logically are more taxing for PCs - <i>'On normal day, one drink from the neck is good. On those intense combats, every few minutes I need one.'</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2024, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T22:34:19-07:00","id":1543732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543724#post1543724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But honestly, the answer remains &quot;how much versimilitude is enough for your play group?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, but my point is that the hard rules from the other games make it into a hard math exercise - and this is what makes this problem pop out so frequently.<br /> <br /> Also, that being the answer doesn\u2019t solve the problem. While verisimilitude isn\u2019t the same requirement from group to group (and isn\u2019t actual \u2018realism\u2019), it can be quite a mood killer for some players, so I think it is a legitimate concern, even if there\u2019s no actual right answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T23:04:59-07:00","id":1543735,"title":"","content":"Of course, drinking blood every game session has more to do with playing the game than realistically modeling how much nourishment a vampire requires. I could perhaps see some justification for it though. If a game session lasts for only 30 minutes of in game time, it probably means that a lot is happening during those 30 minutes. Combat, stressful situations, etc. If, on the other hand, the session lasts for weeks of in game time, then not much is happening over the course of those weeks and the Hungry isn\u2019t consuming much energy. The multi week session might also include some off screen feeding that doesn\u2019t need to be handled in game.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still not sure (and maybe none of us are) about how much blood (or life force) is taken from a feeding and if multiple Curse Dice can be gained from draining the vessel drier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 10-14-2024, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T04:01:49-07:00","id":1543742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543735#post1543735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m still not sure (and maybe none of us are) about how much blood (or life force) is taken from a feeding and if multiple Curse Dice can be gained from draining the vessel drier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 99% sure current official rules are &quot;it's up to the table&quot; and &quot;only if in doing so you satisfy a personal or Family feeding preference, or trigger a Torment.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T06:07:07-07:00","id":1543747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543375-how-many-cursed-in-a-city?p=1543732#post1543732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, but my point is that the hard rules from the other games make it into a hard math exercise - and this is what makes this problem pop out so frequently.<br /> <br /> Also, that being the answer doesn\u2019t solve the problem. While verisimilitude isn\u2019t the same requirement from group to group (and isn\u2019t actual \u2018realism\u2019), it can be quite a mood killer for some players, so I think it is a legitimate concern, even if there\u2019s no actual right answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the hard rules from the other games make it *feel* like a hard maths exercise when in reality there are too many variables and too many assumptions to actually get meaningful answers.<br /> <br /> You could treat it like a Fermi problem but even then your results are likely to change by several orders of magnitude. <br /> <br /> And then in Curseborne not only do you have no hard rules for feeding, you also have no baked in assumption about the Masquerade. You could literally have a town in Curseborne where *half* the population are vampires and it would break no core assumptions of the game. It'd stretch things for that to apply globally but at the local level it's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}